I've run into another variant of this issue. I'm using knitr 1.5 and evaluate 0.5.1, the most recent ones on cran.

With this minimal vignette, and the attached file:

\documentclass{article}
\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}

\begin{document}

Here is a code chunk.

<<foo>>=
if(!require(qpgraph))
{
  source("http://bioconductor.org/biocLite.R")
  biocLite("qpgraph")
  library(qpgraph)
}
load("~/Downloads/cross.rda")
cross
@

You can also write inline expressions, e.g. $\pi=\Sexpr{pi}$, and \Sexpr{1.598673e8} is a big number.

\end{document}

...I get:

Quitting from lines 8-16 (minimal.Rnw)

