Ok guys, after getting some help on stackoverflow and playing around myself, I think I've found the solution....for any newbies like myself here's what you have to do, because knitr basically requires you to reproduce everything, you've done to get to your results and it allows you to work with relative paths, better than absolute paths.

\begin{document}
\title{My first Knitr Output File}
\author{Oliver M. Fisher, MD}
\maketitle{BMI Category Crosstabulation}

<<>>=
read.delim("~/relativepathtofile")
MIC1ELISANEW<-read.table("~/relativepathtofile", header=T)
@

<<>>=
attach(MIC1ELISANEW)
tab1=table(BMICat, Diagnosis)
tab1
summary(tab1)
@

<<>>=
tab1=table(MIC1ELISANEW$BMICat, MIC1ELISANEW$Diagnosis)
summary(tab1)
@

\end{document}

This'll get it to work.

Cheers,

O.

